### Summary

When a real SQLite entry write invalidates an in-flight automatic session-maintenance plan, replacement reclamation starts immediately instead of waiting for the documented one-second quiet window.


### Steps to reproduce


1. Use the tested source commit listed below with development dependencies installed.
2. Save the following test as `src/config/sessions/issue-maintenance-quiet-window.test.ts`.
3. Run from the repository root:

```sh
node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/config/sessions/issue-maintenance-quiet-window.test.ts
```

The test creates a real SQLite session store, inserts an active session and an older eligible session, starts automatic maintenance, and commits another real entry write at the reclamation dispatch boundary. It records when replacement reclamation starts. Date and timeout scheduling are controlled; the production reclamation implementation runs in-process.

```ts
