### Summary

Let Feishu use `channels.feishu.streaming.mode: "progress"` with the same `streaming.progress` sub-config that Slack, Discord, Telegram, Matrix, Mattermost, and MS Teams already support, so operators can watch tool calls, reasoning, and commentary update in a single streaming card instead of only seeing partial reply text.

### Problem to solve

I was comparing streaming behavior across channels and noticed Feishu is the only major channel stuck on two modes. Its config schema hardcodes:

```ts
// extensions/feishu/src/config-schema.ts:102
mode: z.enum(["off", "partial"]).optional(),
```

while every other first-party channel pulls from the shared enum that includes `progress`:

```ts
// src/config/zod-schema.channel-messaging-common.ts:23
export const UnifiedStreamingModeSchema = z.enum(["off", "partial", "block", "progress"]);
```

In `partial` mode (Feishu's default), the streaming card shows live reply text as the model generates it. That's fine for short answers, but during a tool-heavy run — say the agent is running shell commands, reading files, or working through a plan — the Feishu card just sits there with partial text. You can't tell which tool is executing, what command is running, or how far along a plan is. Switch the same agent to Slack or Discord and you get all of that through the progress draft compositor.

I checked why. Feishu's reply dispatcher never calls `createChannelProgressDraftCompositor`. Six other channels do:

| Channel | `progress` mode | compositor wired |
|---------|:-:|:-:|
| Slack | ✅ | `extensions/slack/src/monitor/message-handler/dispatch-progress.ts` |
| Discord | ✅ | `extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler/draft-preview.ts` |
| Telegram | ✅ | `extensions/telegram/src/bot-message-dispatch-progress.ts` |
| Matrix | ✅ | `extensions/matrix/src/matrix/monitor/handler-draft-controller.ts` |
| Mattermost | ✅ | `extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/monitor-turn.ts` |
| MS Teams | ✅ | `extensions/msteams/src/reply-stream-controller.ts` |
| **Feishu** | **—** | **—** |

This isn't a "nice to have." For teams whose primary channel is Feishu, the messaging channel is the interface. Every other major channel shows structured progress; Feishu shows partial text and a typing reaction.

### Proposed solution

Migrate `FeishuStreamingSchema` to `ChannelPreviewStreamingConfigSchema` (or `.extend()` it the way Discord and Slack do). That single change picks up `"block"` and `"progress"` modes plus the `progress` sub-config. Then wire `createChannelProgressDraftCompositor` into the Feishu reply dispatcher's streaming-card update path, following the same pattern Telegram uses.

Config would look like:

```json5
{
  channels: {
    feishu: {
      streaming: {
        mode: "progress",
        progress: {
          label: "Agent",
          maxLines: 8,
          maxLineChars: 280,
          toolProgress: true,
          commandText: "raw",
          commentary: true,
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
```

Defaults and compatibility:

- Default mode stays `"partial"`. Existing configs don't change behavior.
- The `progress` block is optional. Omitted fields fall back to the same defaults other channels use.
- The existing `block` sub-config (`enabled`, `coalesce`) stays valid — `ChannelPreviewStreamingConfigSchema` already includes it.
- Legacy boolean `streaming` and flat keys keep migrating through the existing alias migration in `extensions/feishu/src/doctor-contract.ts`.

The technical pieces are already there. `FeishuStreamingCard.update(text: string)` at `extensions/feishu/src/streaming-card.ts:564` takes full card text and pushes it through Card Kit with sequence-based updates — same replace-the-whole-draft contract the compositor's `update` callback expects. The `start()` / `stop()` lifecycle already manages the streaming card session. And `createChannelProgressDraftCompositor` (`src/channels/progress-draft-compositor.ts:56`) is a drop-in that other channels call with `entry`, `mode`, `update`, and `buildProgressEventLine` — all things Feishu can supply.

### Alternatives considered

**Third-party plugin.** Doesn't work. The streaming config schema is in core `src/config/`, the compositor is in core `src/channels/`, and Feishu is a first-party bundled extension. An external plugin can't add a streaming mode to a bundled channel — the dispatch path and card lifecycle are internal to the extension.

**Stick with `partial` mode and typing reactions.** Typing signals the agent is alive but not what it's doing. You still can't see which tool is running or whether a long command is still executing. That's exactly the gap `progress` mode fills on every other channel.

**Increase the streaming card update frequency.** Faster updates just refresh the same partial reply text faster. They don't add tool names, command detail, reasoning labels, or plan steps — none of that appears in `partial` mode at any frequency.

### Impact

Affected: Feishu channel operators — a primary channel for teams in China and across Asia.

Severity: Medium. Workflow friction and reduced observability, not data loss.

Frequency: Every agent run that involves tool calls, shell commands, or multi-step reasoning — the common case.

Consequence: Operators monitoring agent work through Feishu see partial reply text with no tool progress, reasoning, or plan status. The same agent activity renders with full structured progress on six other channels, making Feishu a second-class surface for real-time observability.

### Evidence/examples

Feishu's streaming schema only accepts `off` and `partial`:

```ts
// extensions/feishu/src/config-schema.ts:100-108
const FeishuStreamingSchema = z
  .object({
    mode: z.enum(["off", "partial"]).optional(),
    chunkMode: z.enum(["length", "newline"]).optional(),
    block: z
      .object({
        enabled: z.boolean().optional(),
        coalesce: BlockStreamingCoalesceSchema,
      })
      .strict()
      .optional(),
  })
  .strict()
  .optional();
```

The shared schema every other channel extends:

```ts
// src/config/zod-schema.channel-messaging-common.ts:23,31-52
export const UnifiedStreamingModeSchema = z.enum(["off", "partial", "block", "progress"]);

export const ChannelStreamingProgressSchema = z
  .object({
    label: z.union([z.string(), z.literal(false)]).optional(),
    labels: z.array(z.string()).optional(),
    maxLines: z.number().int().positive().optional(),
    maxLineChars: z.number().int().positive().optional(),
    render: z.enum(["text", "rich"]).optional(),
    toolProgress: z.boolean().optional(),
    commandText: z.enum(["raw", "status"]).optional(),
    commentary: z.boolean().optional(),
    narration: z.boolean().optional(),
  })
  .strict();

export const ChannelPreviewStreamingConfigSchema = z
  .object({
    mode: UnifiedStreamingModeSchema.optional(),
    chunkMode: TextChunkModeSchema.optional(),
    preview: ChannelStreamingPreviewSchema.optional(),
    progress: ChannelStreamingProgressSchema.optional(),
    block: ChannelStreamingBlockSchema.optional(),
  })
  .strict();
```

Feishu's streaming card already has the update contract the compositor needs:

```ts
// extensions/feishu/src/streaming-card.ts:564
async update(text: string): Promise<void> {
  if (!this.state || this.closed || !text) {
    return;
  }
  this.state.currentText = text;
  this.pendingText = text;
  // ... throttled Card Kit streaming update
}
```

Discord wires the compositor the same way Feishu would:

```ts
// extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.draft-preview.ts:118-131
const progressDraft = createChannelProgressDraftCompositor({
  entry: params.discordConfig,
  mode: discordStreamMode,
  active: Boolean(draftStream),
  seed: progressSeed,
  reasoningLinePrefix: "🧠 ",
  commentaryLinePrefix: "💬 ",
  buildProgressEventLine: (input, options) =>
    input.event === "tool" || input.event === "item"
      ? buildChannelProgressDraftLineForEntry(params.discordConfig, input, options)
      : buildChannelProgressDraftLine(input, options),
  update: async (previewText, options) => {
    lastPartialText = previewText;
    draftStream?.update(previewText);
    // ...
  },
});
```

### Do you plan to open a PR for this?

No, proposing the idea only

### Additional information

- Default mode stays `"partial"`; existing configs are unchanged.
- The `progress` sub-config should reuse `ChannelStreamingProgressSchema` so Feishu doesn't diverge from other channels.
- No new Gateway API, SQLite, or protocol surface — the compositor and schema already exist in core.
- Legacy boolean `streaming` and flat keys should keep migrating through the existing alias migration in `extensions/feishu/src/doctor-contract.ts`.
- This is not a duplicate of #65228. That issue asked for general liveness feedback (typing, heartbeats) and was closed as already implemented. This one asks for the specific `progress` streaming mode and `streaming.progress` sub-config that six other channels already implement through the shared compositor — Feishu still does not have it.

