## What Problem This Solves

Heading-only memory files can merge CJK headings into embedding chunks that exceed the chunker’s weighted character budget.

Related: #198958

## Why This Change Was Made

Heading repair now uses the same CJK-aware estimator as `createMarkdownChunker`. The chunking identity advances from v6 to v7 so unchanged v6 indexes are rebuilt.

## User Impact

Heading-heavy memory files stay within the configured weighted chunk budget, and existing indexes receive the corrected boundaries on upgrade.

## Evidence

- The same three-heading corpus ran against the pinned validation base e4f55593741ed56f9bac9196847bb079f25c8d75 and this PR head. Base v6 merged it into one raw-29 / weighted-92 chunk; the 32-unit proxy returned HTTP 400 before model forwarding and published zero rows. PR-head search upgraded the existing v6 index to three weighted-30 chunks.
- Separate legacy-v6 compatibility run at 847611dcaa3bf0e2783335f961dd1fd0580e4d9f stored one embedded chunk plus source, provenance, recall metadata, and settings 8/0. Isolated doctor --fix migrated SQLite schema 27 → 42 while the v6 text/hash, embedding, settings, source, provenance, and recall rows stayed intact. PR-head search then rebuilt that same database as v7 with three embedded chunks and a valid index identity.
- The production manager and HTTP embedding client used real 1024-dimensional vectors from Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-GGUF:Q8_0, served locally by llama-server. Search for 物理课程与力学 ranked that heading first (score=0.804, vectorScore=0.886). This proves local model inference and vector-backed retrieval, not a hosted-provider request.
- Supplementary shipped-CLI run launched node openclaw.mjs memory search in a separate process with isolated config and state. It exited 0, returned memory/syllabus.md with the requested physics heading in the snippet, and forwarded two real 1024-dimensional model inputs. CLI uses its normal chunk defaults; because public config has no 8/0 override, the strict 32-unit comparison remains on the manager seam.
- Exact-head negative control: with the manager's internal chunk-token seam set to 80, the 92-unit chunk received HTTP 400, made zero model calls, and published zero rows. The proxy uses the same production estimateStringChars CJK-weighting helper as the chunker. The normal proof uses 8/0; public config has no chunk-size override.
- Focused validation already run for this head: 3 files, 33 tests passed, including the weighted merge regression and v6-to-v7 upgrade.

