The matching path performs two call lookups before bridge entry: the initial resolution, and the live-call recheck after admission persistence. The test now expects both. The mismatch path still requires zero lookups, events, and bridges.

With only the production changes of this pull request reversed (`webhook.ts`, `realtime-handler.ts`, `realtime-inbound-admission.ts`) and every test left in place, the same file fails all three tests; with the changes restored it passes 3/3.

The remaining behavioral test doubles are the external `RealtimeVoiceProviderPlugin` and its `RealtimeVoiceBridge`; manager spies are call-through observers.

### Rebase onto current main

The branch is rebased onto current main. Main had since split the realtime inbound admission logic out of `webhook.ts`; the initial-TwiML-request classification now lives beside it as `getRealtimeTwimlParams` in `realtime-inbound-admission.ts`, which keeps `webhook.ts` under its line cap. The binding behavior is unchanged: a signed `CallSid` is required and trimmed before stream issuance, recorded on the one-time session, and compared against the Twilio start frame before lookup or bridge creation. Telnyx keeps its internal-call binding.

Existing fixtures that started Twilio sessions without a matching provider call identity now supply one. The boundary test is registered with the database-worker test configuration because it uses the SQLite store. `config/test-lines-allocations/136506-signed-realtime-boundary.txt` requests 49 test lines above the standard allowance for the signed HTTP/WebSocket/SQLite boundary test.

